1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,435
Fingerprints on the screen, crumbs under
the keys,

2
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:06,515
and one wrong move can scratch the display

3
00:00:06,525 --> 00:00:08,079
or damage the keyboard.

4
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:10,993
A clean MacBook takes five minutes.

5
00:00:11,285 --> 00:00:14,456
Seven safe steps, with just a cloth and

6
00:00:14,466 --> 00:00:15,486
a little water.

7
00:00:16,451 --> 00:00:20,630
Stay for step three: it's where most
damage happens.

8
00:00:21,233 --> 00:00:22,196
WikiTube.

9
00:00:22,429 --> 00:00:24,773
Whatever it is, here's how.

10
00:00:25,067 --> 00:00:27,379
A MacBook is easy to clean if you

11
00:00:27,389 --> 00:00:30,177
respect two rules: use as little liquid as

12
00:00:30,187 --> 00:00:34,076
possible, and never spray anything
directly onto the computer.

13
00:00:34,436 --> 00:00:38,104
Moisture in the keyboard or the speakers
causes real damage.

14
00:00:38,465 --> 00:00:41,808
We'll follow Apple's own advice, step by
step,

15
00:00:41,936 --> 00:00:43,375
in good light.

16
00:00:43,933 --> 00:00:47,128
You'll need two microfiber cloths, a
little distilled

17
00:00:47,138 --> 00:00:50,518
water, a can of compressed air, and, to

18
00:00:50,528 --> 00:00:54,648
disinfect the outside, seventy percent
isopropyl wipes.

19
00:00:54,881 --> 00:00:56,529
No household sprays.

20
00:00:57,067 --> 00:00:58,076
Step one.

21
00:00:58,878 --> 00:01:01,747
Before you clean anything, turn the
MacBook off

22
00:01:01,757 --> 00:01:06,586
completely, and unplug the charger and any
cables or accessories.

23
00:01:06,947 --> 00:01:09,712
A powered-off computer can't be damaged by
a

24
00:01:09,722 --> 00:01:12,602
stray drop of moisture, and you'll see
dust

25
00:01:12,612 --> 00:01:15,607
and smudges more clearly on a dark screen.

26
00:01:16,571 --> 00:01:18,477
Let the laptop cool down if it has

27
00:01:18,487 --> 00:01:19,728
been working hard.

28
00:01:20,089 --> 00:01:22,447
Then place it on a clean, flat surface

29
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:23,606
with good light.

30
00:01:24,059 --> 00:01:26,592
This only takes thirty seconds, but it is

31
00:01:26,602 --> 00:01:29,402
the step that protects your computer, so
please

32
00:01:29,412 --> 00:01:30,386
don't skip it.

33
00:01:30,747 --> 00:01:32,954
If you use an external monitor or a

34
00:01:32,964 --> 00:01:35,297
mouse, unplug those too.

35
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:36,842
Step two.

36
00:01:37,505 --> 00:01:40,943
Take a dry, soft microfiber cloth and wipe

37
00:01:40,953 --> 00:01:44,864
the screen gently in one direction, from
top to bottom.

38
00:01:45,527 --> 00:01:48,779
Dry wiping removes dust and grit first, so

39
00:01:48,789 --> 00:01:50,718
you won't drag them across the glass when

40
00:01:50,728 --> 00:01:51,923
you add moisture.

41
00:01:52,284 --> 00:01:55,002
Use light pressure, and don't press hard
on

42
00:01:55,012 --> 00:01:58,149
the display, because the panel is thin and

43
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:00,062
pressure can leave marks.

44
00:02:00,724 --> 00:02:04,464
Don't use paper towels, tissues or kitchen
cloths,

45
00:02:04,474 --> 00:02:06,763
which have rough fibres that can leave
tiny

46
00:02:06,773 --> 00:02:08,293
scratches over time.

47
00:02:09,095 --> 00:02:12,312
A good microfiber cloth lasts for years
and

48
00:02:12,322 --> 00:02:13,378
can be washed.

49
00:02:13,924 --> 00:02:16,225
Always check the cloth is clean before you

50
00:02:16,235 --> 00:02:19,383
start, because one trapped grain of sand
can

51
00:02:19,393 --> 00:02:20,773
scratch the screen.

52
00:02:21,924 --> 00:02:25,580
Now for the fingerprints that dry wiping
leaves behind.

53
00:02:26,133 --> 00:02:27,293
Step three.

54
00:02:27,654 --> 00:02:31,266
For fingerprints that remain, slightly
dampen a clean

55
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:33,470
microfiber cloth with water.

56
00:02:34,133 --> 00:02:37,745
It should be barely damp, not wet, so

57
00:02:37,755 --> 00:02:39,577
squeeze out any excess.

58
00:02:40,379 --> 00:02:42,853
Wipe the screen gently in the same top

59
00:02:42,863 --> 00:02:44,070
to bottom motion.

60
00:02:45,034 --> 00:02:48,589
Apple recommends water only for its
displays, so

61
00:02:48,599 --> 00:02:52,780
skip window cleaners, alcohol, vinegar,
and any

62
00:02:52,790 --> 00:02:56,528
household sprays, which can strip the
anti-glare coating.

63
00:02:57,492 --> 00:03:01,369
Never spray liquid directly onto the
screen or the keyboard.

64
00:03:01,730 --> 00:03:04,019
If you see a stubborn spot, go over

65
00:03:04,029 --> 00:03:08,358
it again with the damp cloth, gently,
without scrubbing.

66
00:03:09,323 --> 00:03:12,227
Patience works better than pressure, and a
clean

67
00:03:12,237 --> 00:03:14,535
screen only takes a minute.

68
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,074
Step four.

69
00:03:16,621 --> 00:03:18,851
Go over the screen with your second, dry

70
00:03:18,861 --> 00:03:22,680
microfiber cloth, using the same gentle
strokes.

71
00:03:23,134 --> 00:03:26,607
This removes any moisture left behind, and
stops

72
00:03:26,617 --> 00:03:27,963
streaks from forming.

73
00:03:28,626 --> 00:03:30,705
Then tilt the lid toward a window or

74
00:03:30,715 --> 00:03:33,201
lamp, and look along the surface at an

75
00:03:33,211 --> 00:03:37,216
angle, where streaks and missed spots are
easiest to see.

76
00:03:38,018 --> 00:03:40,527
If you spot any, repeat the damp and

77
00:03:40,537 --> 00:03:43,671
dry steps lightly on just that area.

78
00:03:44,125 --> 00:03:45,891
Leave the lid open for a minute so

79
00:03:45,901 --> 00:03:49,894
any trace of moisture evaporates, before
you close the MacBook.

80
00:03:50,347 --> 00:03:53,275
This final check also protects the
keyboard from

81
00:03:53,285 --> 00:03:55,652
marking the screen when the lid closes.

82
00:03:56,013 --> 00:03:59,275
With the screen done, it's time for the
keyboard.

83
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:00,958
Step five.

84
00:04:01,319 --> 00:04:03,944
Hold the MacBook at about a seventy-five
degree

85
00:04:03,954 --> 00:04:06,786
angle, so the keys tilt toward you.

86
00:04:07,449 --> 00:04:09,865
Using the thin straw on the compressed air

87
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:13,290
can, spray in short bursts across the
keyboard

88
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:15,192
in a left to right motion.

89
00:04:15,854 --> 00:04:18,387
Rotate the MacBook to its right side and

90
00:04:18,397 --> 00:04:21,510
repeat, then to its left side and repeat

91
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:22,587
one more time.

92
00:04:23,250 --> 00:04:26,140
Keep the can upright, and don't shake it,

93
00:04:26,269 --> 00:04:27,998
so no liquid comes out.

94
00:04:28,962 --> 00:04:32,142
This lifts crumbs and dust from under the
keys.

95
00:04:32,503 --> 00:04:35,245
Never use a vacuum cleaner, since static
can

96
00:04:35,255 --> 00:04:36,415
harm the computer.

97
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:39,877
If a key still feels stuck afterwards,
repeat

98
00:04:39,887 --> 00:04:42,513
the process once more, and book a service

99
00:04:42,523 --> 00:04:44,519
visit if it doesn't improve.

100
00:04:45,067 --> 00:04:46,157
Step six.

101
00:04:46,611 --> 00:04:49,341
Lightly dampen a corner of your cloth, or

102
00:04:49,351 --> 00:04:52,951
use a seventy percent isopropyl alcohol
wipe, and

103
00:04:52,961 --> 00:04:55,236
wipe the keys and the trackpad.

104
00:04:55,782 --> 00:04:58,001
Apple says these wipes are fine on the

105
00:04:58,011 --> 00:05:00,205
outside surfaces of the computer.

106
00:05:00,751 --> 00:05:04,654
Work key by key, using light pressure, and

107
00:05:04,664 --> 00:05:08,134
keep any moisture out of the gaps between
the keys.

108
00:05:08,681 --> 00:05:11,745
Don't use bleach or hydrogen peroxide.

109
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,903
If a key is sticky, wipe it a second time.

110
00:05:15,449 --> 00:05:17,378
This is also a good moment to clean

111
00:05:17,388 --> 00:05:20,743
the palm rests, where oils from your hands
build up.

112
00:05:21,289 --> 00:05:24,205
Avoid getting wet cloths near the ports,
the

113
00:05:24,215 --> 00:05:26,501
speaker holes and the fan vents.

114
00:05:27,303 --> 00:05:29,148
One step is left:

115
00:05:30,299 --> 00:05:32,771
the case, and a few habits.

116
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,377
Step seven.

117
00:05:34,924 --> 00:05:37,537
Finish by wiping the outside case and the

118
00:05:37,547 --> 00:05:41,017
bottom with the damp cloth, avoiding the
ports,

119
00:05:41,146 --> 00:05:43,235
speaker grilles and vents.

120
00:05:44,037 --> 00:05:45,812
Then build a few habits.

121
00:05:46,475 --> 00:05:49,017
Wash and dry your hands before you work,

122
00:05:49,250 --> 00:05:51,408
and avoid eating over the keyboard.

123
00:05:52,373 --> 00:05:55,553
Wipe the screen once a week with the dry
cloth.

124
00:05:56,703 --> 00:05:59,491
And before closing the lid, make sure
nothing

125
00:05:59,501 --> 00:06:01,787
is on the keyboard, such as a pen

126
00:06:01,846 --> 00:06:04,309
or a camera cover thicker than a sheet

127
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:08,161
of paper, since these can mark or crack
the display.

128
00:06:08,522 --> 00:06:11,008
A two minute weekly wipe keeps your Mac

129
00:06:11,018 --> 00:06:14,628
looking new, and helps its resale value as
well.

130
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:18,881
If a smudge stays, your cloth is probably
the problem.

131
00:06:19,242 --> 00:06:22,297
A dirty cloth just moves grease around, so

132
00:06:22,307 --> 00:06:25,095
use a fresh one, and wash used cloths

133
00:06:25,105 --> 00:06:28,134
with mild soap and no fabric softener.

134
00:06:29,285 --> 00:06:31,617
Never scrape a mark with a fingernail.

135
00:06:32,582 --> 00:06:34,847
Faint marks may be wear on the coating,

136
00:06:34,857 --> 00:06:37,004
which no cleaning will remove.

137
00:06:37,567 --> 00:06:40,875
If keys stick or stop working after
cleaning,

138
00:06:40,968 --> 00:06:44,055
ask Apple or an authorized service
provider.

139
00:06:44,416 --> 00:06:46,879
The same goes for lines or dead spots

140
00:06:46,889 --> 00:06:47,979
on the display.

141
00:06:48,433 --> 00:06:51,105
If the case bulges or the trackpad seems

142
00:06:51,115 --> 00:06:53,891
to lift, stop using the laptop and have

143
00:06:53,901 --> 00:06:57,964
the battery checked, because a swollen
battery can be unsafe.

144
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:01,172
Keep a clean microfiber cloth in a small

145
00:07:01,182 --> 00:07:05,070
pouch in your bag, so grit never scratches
the screen.

146
00:07:05,617 --> 00:07:07,891
Replace the cloth when it looks worn.

147
00:07:08,183 --> 00:07:09,949
Do not leave the laptop in a hot

148
00:07:09,959 --> 00:07:13,049
car or in direct sun for hours, and

149
00:07:13,059 --> 00:07:15,322
carry it in a padded sleeve.

150
00:07:15,867 --> 00:07:18,095
Let's go through the mistakes to avoid.

151
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:22,821
First, never spray any liquid directly on
the MacBook.

152
00:07:23,112 --> 00:07:25,584
It can flow into the keyboard and speakers

153
00:07:25,677 --> 00:07:28,776
and cause damage that isn't covered by
warranty.

154
00:07:29,927 --> 00:07:33,725
Second, don't use glass cleaner, bleach,
vinegar or

155
00:07:33,735 --> 00:07:37,275
aerosols, as they can strip the coating
from the screen.

156
00:07:37,636 --> 00:07:40,723
And third, don't scrub or press hard.

157
00:07:41,386 --> 00:07:43,907
A gentle touch and a clean cloth beat

158
00:07:43,917 --> 00:07:46,844
force every time, and the display can be

159
00:07:46,854 --> 00:07:48,571
marked easily by pressure.

160
00:07:48,932 --> 00:07:50,385
If you ever spill a drink on the

161
00:07:50,395 --> 00:07:53,622
keyboard, switch it off at once, unplug
it,

162
00:07:53,750 --> 00:07:57,534
and contact Apple, before you try to clean
it yourself.

163
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:01,025
Let's go through the whole routine one
more time.

164
00:08:01,479 --> 00:08:03,602
Shut down and unplug.

165
00:08:04,149 --> 00:08:06,412
Dust the screen with a dry cloth.

166
00:08:06,958 --> 00:08:09,326
Wipe with a barely damp cloth.

167
00:08:10,476 --> 00:08:12,646
Dry it and check for streaks.

168
00:08:13,193 --> 00:08:15,735
Clear crumbs with short bursts of air.

169
00:08:16,885 --> 00:08:19,043
Wipe the keys and trackpad.

170
00:08:19,404 --> 00:08:22,468
And keep the Mac clean with a few small
habits.

171
00:08:23,270 --> 00:08:26,941
Seven steps, five minutes, and a MacBook
that

172
00:08:26,951 --> 00:08:28,134
looks cared for.

173
00:08:29,098 --> 00:08:33,338
The bonus sections cover stubborn marks,
Apple and daily

174
00:08:33,348 --> 00:08:34,055
care.

175
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:38,314
That's how you clean a MacBook screen and
keyboard safely.

176
